  "consumer": "Hermes plugin (crates/cli/src/hermes_integration/assets/pohunek)",
  "capture": "A throwaway python3 driver (not checked in) loads the v0.33.0 plugin package like tests/test_plugin_runtime.py does, builds HookReporter(env) with env {POHUNEK_ENV=1, POHUNEK_SESSION_ID=ses_0123456789abcdef, POHUNEK_RUNTIME_ID=rt-0123456789abcdef, POHUNEK_SOCKET_PATH=<capture socket>, POHUNEK_PROTOCOL_VERSION=3, POHUNEK_DAEMON_ID=daemon-0123456789ab} (no POHUNEK_WORKER_SOCKET_PATH, so the public fallback is used) and calls callbacks(reporter): on_session_start({session_id}), pre_llm_call, pre_approval_request, post_approval_response, post_llm_call, on_session_end({interrupted:true}), on_session_finalize against a throwaway python3 capture server (unix socket, one NDJSON request per line, logs the raw line, replies with a canned protocol-3 envelope {\"v\":3,\"id\":<echo>,\"ok\":...} so the consumer proceeds; not checked in) listening on $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pohunek/daemon.sock. `cli_invocations` come from Tools(policy, session).handlers() (policy mode full, pohunek_cli = a recorder script that appends sys.argv to a file) for pohunek_session_output/wait/get/screen; `args` is the tool input, `argv` the exact CLI argv the plugin built. Normalized values: the process pid (4242), its process start identity (1234567) and expires_at (2026-01-01T00:00:30Z) vary per run; request ids and sequences are deterministic and untouched.",
